{% doc %}
  Renders one OFFICIAL Montibello Luxlight icon, reproduced from the exact
  SVG assets served on the live official PDP (hair.montibello.com/wp-content/
  uploads/2025/12/*.svg — confirmed via a live DOM audit of the Supreme
  Control Oil PDP: each icon's own <img src> was inspected directly). These
  are NOT this theme's generic `snippets/icon.liquid` line-icon set — the
  official Montibello icon language uses its own solid/filled shapes with
  their own native aspect ratios, so each case below keeps its own
  `viewBox`/`width`/`height` rather than being forced into the theme's
  shared 20x20 outline-icon wrapper (doing that would stretch/distort them).

  Source → official filename:
  - format          → format-icon.svg              (bottle/container silhouette)
  - hair_type       → icono-tipo-de-cabello.svg     (head/hair silhouette)
  - technology      → icono-ingrediente-principal.svg (badge/seal shape)
  - ingredients     → icono-ingredientes.svg        (molecular/flower shape)
  - how_to          → icono-como-usar.svg           (open book)
  - interest_data   → icono-check.svg               (outlined check-circle)

  `fill="black"`/`stroke="black"` on the original paths are intentionally
  left in place — CSS `fill: currentColor` / `stroke: currentColor` declared
  on `.montibello-luxlight-icon svg *` in the caller's stylesheet overrides
  them (a real stylesheet rule beats a presentation attribute), so no
  colors needed to be hand-edited out of the official path data.

  @param {string} icon - one of: format, hair_type, technology, ingredients, how_to, interest_data
{% enddoc %}

